# What git is for here: the code, the documents, and the RECORDS — the
# irreplaceable human judgement. 74 observation records took a lot of looking
# and nothing can regenerate them.
#
# What it is not for: 2 GB of binaries that are either raw input or
# reproducible output.

# Raw input. 715 MB of originals, and they came from zips Geno still has in
# Google Photos. Losing git would not lose these; putting them in git would
# make it unusable.
photos/

# The source zips, already processed. 786 MB.
archive/zips/
archive/unzipped/
archive/staging/

# Disposable and regenerable by `python3 pipeline/run.py`. 564 MB.
work/

# Fetched on demand by providers/yolox.py. 34 MB.
pipeline/models/*.onnx

# Derived: regenerated by the detector in minutes. See analysis/README.md.
analysis/derived/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
staging/
